WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.400
. This next story is a political story, but
it's also sort of a math story.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.250
You know, I love a good math story.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:11.020
And this math story has to do with the fact
that a lot of people don't understand percentage

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.660
versus percentage points.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.790
Now, to people who do understand the difference.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:19.240
Please accept my sincere apology that I have
to do this right now.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.330
But the amount of confusion over this over
the last 24 hours has forced my hand and I

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.330
have to do this.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.580
So here's the headline.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.779
Donald Trump's approval rating is down 10
points.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:34.110
Or you could also say 10 percentage points
in the last month.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:38.820
So early in the Corona virus pandemic, Donald
Trump's approval actually went up all the

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.960
way up to 49 percent in the Gallup tracking
poll.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.830
It is now down to 39 percent.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:47.530
So Trump's approval went from 49 percent to
39 percent.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.710
That's a decline of 10 points.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:55.600
The problem here is that some people don't
understand the difference between percent

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.710
and percentage points.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:03.410
Others understand the concept, but are using
the wrong term and just confusing other people.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.170
So let's just work through a very quick example.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.980
If someone has 50 percent approval and their
approval goes down by 10 percent.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:17.980
Strictly speaking, that would mean 50 percent,
10 percent of fifty is five.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:21.870
That means if you have 50 percent approval
and approval goes down 10 percent, you go

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:22.940
from 50 to 45.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.370
OK, 10 percent.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.550
A 50 is five.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:34.290
So far, I think, reclear, if you have an approval
of 50 percent and it drops 10 points.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.080
Also said 10 percentage points.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.170
That's a decline of 10 actual points.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.479
Meaning you went from 50 to 40.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:44.190
You lost 10 points.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.200
Fifty minus 10 is 40.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:52.740
The confusion comes when we're talking about
percent changes to things already measured

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.860
in percent.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:54.860
OK.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:59.820
So in this case, are real world numbers are
Trump's approval spiked to forty nine and

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.880
then dropped to thirty nine in a one month
period.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.990
That's a ten point decline.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:09.539
But it is about a 20 percent decline to his
approval.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:10.539
Right.

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:15.790
If you lose ten out of forty nine, that's
about 20 percent.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.660
And if you're now thoroughly confused, forget
everything I've said.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:25.370
The news part of this story is that Trump's
approval went from forty nine to thirty nine.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.500
That's a very rapid decline.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.780
In fact, I think it's the largest one month
decline that Trump has seen at anytime during

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.780
his presidency.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.640
Now there's good news and there's bad news.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.860
The good news is that.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.000
Clearly, Donald Trump's approval is not immune
from his actions.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.170
In other words, the failed coronavirus response.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:46.700
The totalitarian instincts that came to light
after the George Floyd killing and the protests

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.370
that started this has hurt Donald Trump.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:50.370
That's good.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.780
He's not immune.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:57.510
The bad news is that somehow four out of 10
Americans still think he's doing a good job.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:02.611
So this may be a good time to remind you that
when it comes to presidential approval, when

00:03:02.611 --> 00:03:06.800
you think about how divided the country is.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.040
Presidential approval adds up to a hundred,
but there's not really a hundred points of

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.770
approval in play.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:16.569
There's some portion of people who, for ideological
reasons, will never approve of the job that

00:03:16.569 --> 00:03:17.569
the president does.

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:20.410
I don't know if that's like, you know, 10
percent, 15 percent, 20.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:21.730
I'm not really sure.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.790
On the other side, you've got people who will
never abandon Trump no matter what he does.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:28.349
That could be 15, 20, 25 percent.

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:33.340
I don't know exactly what it is right now,
but the point is, Trump's bottom for approval

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.920
is not zero.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.220
And his top four approval is not 100.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:43.040
Even with George W. Bush, when things were
less partizan after 9/11, Bush saw a massive

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.129
spike in approval to 90 or 88 percent, something
like that.

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:53.740
That was probably his ceiling and those were
the absolutely most extenuating circumstances.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:58.560
So the point is, when Trump's approval moves
from forty nine to thirty nine, forty nine,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.700
thirty nine, it's in that range.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:05.239
It's really a lot more than that because they're
the bottom is not zero and the top is not

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:06.239
100.

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:08.030
Pick what numbers you think it is with Trump.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:12.430
It's probably something like I don't think
he is approval, no matter what he does, would

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:16.530
go below 25 or maybe even 28, something like
that.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.720
And I don't think it would go higher than
probably 80 no matter what he does.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:26.440
So in the context of a range that is more
like 28 to 80, a ten point swing is pretty

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.440
significant.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.330
But there's a lot of people in this country
who will never abandon him.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.100
It might be for their own self esteem.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:36.930
They don't want to admit to themselves that
they made a mistake when they voted Trump

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:37.930
in 2016.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:42.380
And the way to at least trick your brain into
thinking you didn't make a mistake is to vote

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.620
for him again in 2020.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:48.250
There's this quote incorrectly attributed
to Mark Twain.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.170
It's still a good quote, just not Mark Twain.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:56.130
The quote is it's easier to fool people than
to convince them that they've been fooled.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:01.010
And along those lines, we have to understand
why a lot of 2016 Trump voters are going to

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:02.710
vote for him again.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:03.770
Some may abandon him.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.419
And there's a very small margin there that
Trump can afford to lose before it becomes

00:05:07.419 --> 00:05:09.790
almost impossible to win reelection.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:14.520
But understand, it's easier to fool people
than then to convince them they've been fooled.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.410
And it is very relevant in the Times with
Trump.

